WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.670
Explosive Shoot

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.810
Keep fighting chasing your dream

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.140
with love, courage and friendship

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.640
This Blade and I are one

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.680
Spin as hard as you can until the limit

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.780
BURNING SOUL

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.200
The things I can't do alone

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.140
are not impossible if you're with me

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.960
Come with me

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.280
to the ends of this world

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.540
The Four Sacred Beasts are athletes of love

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.100
Shine! Open your eyes!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.730
Dragoon  Dranzer  Draciel  Driger

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.450
Awaken!

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.060
Fly across the sky, my energy

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.380
Rise up, Sacred Beast!

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.830
To defeat all the enemies who stand in our way

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.050
jump, bearing everyone's hopes

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.080
SHINING SOUL

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.670
This town looks very pretty.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.400
Yeah...

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.540
Hey, guys!

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.220
Takao! You finally decided to wake up?

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.840
The ship's docked! Why didn't you tell me?

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.400
Are we in Russia already?

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.770
Of course not.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.650
This is Thrumpton, England.
It's just one of the stops.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.380
Oh, I see.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.280
Huh..?

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.370
What?

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.010
Ralf Jurgens...

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.480
Ralf...

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.500
If we meet him at the World
Tournament, I will get him!

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.790
But it's strange... This ship is on its way to Russia,

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:38.370
so why is he getting off here?

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.240
I've got it!

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.570
He wants to eat breakfast here
while the ship is anchored!

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.080
Eating in the city, huh? Sounds good.
I'm getting tired of the food they serve on board.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.510
Let's go get ourselves breakfast, too.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.730
We don't know how long this ship'll be anchored for...

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.170
I'm not sure if we have the time.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.730
Don't you worry about it!

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:03.630
The ship will be at this port for another six hours.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.500
Is that so?

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.080
Yep.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.770
Then we have all the time we need!

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.530
Let's go have breakfast!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.450
Alright! Can't fight on an empty stomach, anyway!

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.800
Let's eat to our heart's content so we won't lose to that Ralf guy!

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.230
Oh, come on. You don't need to go that far.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.680
Come on, guys!

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.170
Right behind you.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.800
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:35.980
Troubled Journey in Europe!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.940
Excuse me! Wasn't there a ship anchored here?

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.120
It set sail about an hour ago.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.380
S-Set sail?!

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.100
W-W-Why?!

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.710
I thought we had time to spare?!

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:07.460
T-The World Tournament! The Russian Tournament... My dream..!

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:08.690
Calm down.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.620
No point in panicking.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.720
Let's go over our situation.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.920
We were left behind by the ship
we were supposed to be on.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.780
Right?

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.220
Yes...

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.790
That darn geezer lied to us!

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.890
Ferry services aren't that common.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:32.140
So instead of waiting for another ship, we should come up with another way to get there.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.220
Easier said than done.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.230
We don't have much money on us.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:41.390
That's it! We can ask President Daitenji for help. He's waiting in Russia ahead of us!

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.850
You're right!

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:47.640
How could we forget? We have a powerful ally by our side, old man Daitenji!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.940
But I don't know exactly <i>where</i> in Russia he is.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.620
A-Are you serious?!

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:56.230
All he said was that he'd come pick us up when the ship docked.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:59.440
None of us expected that our
schedule would be thrown off like this.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.690
Then what are we supposed to do?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.240
Hey. I know how we can locate the President.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.850
London—England's historic capital.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.330
That's nice and all, but why are we here?

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.850
You see, the BBA's English branch is located here.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.440
The BBA's English branch?

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.930
Yeah, you heard me.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.440
They collect information on various Bladers,

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:36.690
and help out people like me who travel around the globe.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:42.690
They kind of work like an embassy. These offices can be find all over the world.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.040
Oh? I had no idea the BBA operated on such a big scale.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.820
I'm sure we can contact the president from there.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:51.960
Here we are.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.990
I have the displeasure of informing you that
we were unable to contact President Daitenji.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:00.750
Oh no!

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.090
I suppose he's away from the phone right now.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:06.680
In any case, I'll try again later.

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:10.120
Why don't you all stay in London for the day?

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.440
As soon as the President is
available, I'll get in touch with you.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.620
There's no helping it.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.420
I'll arrange hotel reservations for you.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.670
Thank you very much.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:20.700
Hello?

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.480
That's one day down the drain, I guess.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.610
You got that right.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:32.540
This..!

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:36.510
That's Ralf!

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.480
Oh, that picture is from the
Dutch tournament earlier this year.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:44.260
Ralf Jurgens won this year's competition.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.020
The Dutch tournament?

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.540
With that kind of power, it's not surprising.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:53.320
So I guess he <i>will</i> be
present at the Final Tournament...

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.480
No, he's not participating.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.730
Why not?

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:58.700
How come?!

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.490
I'm not quite sure myself.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.600
To think that someone as strong as him isn't in the Tournament...

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.450
What's going on here?

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.910
For now, let's get to the hotel.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:16.460
Still, it looks like the bar for the finals
of the World Tournament is pretty high.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:21.510
In any case, I want to see the power of
those at the World Tournament for myself.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:25.330
The World Tournament... you say?

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.660
What's wrong?

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:38.020
Oh, it was just my imagination.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:47.050
We have to get the President
to show us to our destination.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:52.200
If we took an airplane and flew directly,
we'd definitely make it in time for the Finals.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.450
That's great news.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.540
All is not lost, it seems.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:56.570
Yes!

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:57.940
Say...

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.710
Hear me out. What if, instead of going by plane...

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.800
we took trains, buses, and stuff like that?

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.410
What do you mean?

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.840
What's that? Do you want to go sightseeing, Takao?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.550
No way. If we happened to get into trouble again along the way, we won't make it.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.470
No, that's not what I mean

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:20.190
I want to meet all sorts of opponents.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:21.950
All sorts of opponents?

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.150
European Bladers.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.650
What did you say?!

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:30.840
I've been thinking about it since we left the office.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:36.060
Ralf Jurgens... If someone as strong as him isn't even in the Tournament...

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:41.220
That must mean that guys as strong as him or even stronger are all around Europe.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.720
It's very likely.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.390
Also, his fighting style...

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:51.930
I've never seen someone
control a Sacred Beast like that.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.690
It's a whole new type of Blader.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:58.680
<i>That</i> is why I'm getting fired up!

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.190
If other people like him exist,
we can't possibly ignore them!

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:08.180
Professor, you're the one who said that we'd need all sorts of training to prepare for the finals.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.240
This would be the perfect chance.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.940
But I didn't mean for it to happen like this!

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:18.960
If something goes wrong and we can't make it in
time for the finals, all our efforts will have been vain!

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:22.310
You have a good point.
I understand how you feel, Takao, but...

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:26.920
Right now, our priority is to arrive on time.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.980
Kai, what're you thinking?

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.180
I couldn't care less.

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:33.020
Tch.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.770
This just doesn't sit right with me...

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.230
Dear guests, there's a package for you.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:40.230
Coming!

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:43.930
Here.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.930
Thank you.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.440
What's that?

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:54.020
Weird. There's no sender or recipient here.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:58.660
It's a videotape!

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.660
Ah, Pops!

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:08.630
That guy's my dad!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:09.580
Your dad?

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:14.020
Yeah. He's been away from home because of work. I haven't seen him in some time.

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:16.680
But why is he on this tape?

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:21.930
The archaeological research I've been conducting all this time is finally complete.

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:23.520
Archaeology?

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:27.440
Yeah. He's been traveling the world on an archaeological dig.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.940
Looks like this video was supposed to be a report of some kind.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.890
The results align with my past hypothesis.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:39.660
<i>They</i> existed in the traditions of various cultures.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:44.380
In some places, they are seen as symbols of veneration of past dynasties.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:47.420
In other places, they're viewed as national treasures.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.920
W-What is he talking about?

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:55.840
Each language gives them a different name, but if you translate them, they all have the same meaning.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:59.730
For example, in our language, one would call them 'Sacred Beasts'.

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:01.060
What?!

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.200
Sacred Beasts?!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.490
I had no idea my dad was
researching the Sacred Beasts..!

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:23.720
The legends found in different locations describe the Sacred Beasts as follows;

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:29.370
They assume the shapes of mythological creatures.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:32.720
They seem to reside inside small objects.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:36.680
Some kind of event causes them to appear in a big burst of energy.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:44.450
Bits..!

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.930
Small objects...

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.440
You don't mean..?!

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.440
The logic fits.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:57.050
The Bit of my Driger, Byakko, is something my handed down by my clan through the generations.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:00.590
Now that you mention it, Dragoon's Bit, too...

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:05.000
It comes from the Sword of the Dragon Heart—a family heirloom.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:10.050
Then the Sacred Beasts
mentioned are the ones in the Beys?

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:16.780
In many countries, the Sacred Beasts are perceived as a symbol of great power.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.290
However, in certain European countries,

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:25.140
there was a time where people controlled these Beasts and made them fight each other.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.610
Doesn't that sound just like what Ralf did?

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:34.890
In other regions, the existence of 'evil' Sacred Beasts brought fear to the people.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:38.160
There's little information on this,
and as such, it's the subject of my research.

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:40.130
Evil Sacred Beasts...

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.520
This concludes my report.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.570
I will contact you again if I find anything else.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:00.380
Who would have thought that Takao's dad was researching the Sacred Beasts?

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.390
Still, who in the world sent that video?

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.460
It's hard to tell, but we can always hypothesize.

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:10.460
Whoever sent it wanted us to focus our attention on the Sacred Beasts,

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:15.290
and make us want to find out more about Europe's Bladers.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.910
At least, I think that was their intention.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.800
Well, I can definitely say their plan worked on me.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:23.780
But it feels like we're being
manipulated, and I don't like that.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:28.780
I wonder what the relationship is between the sender and Takao's father?

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:31.760
What do you think, Takao?

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:36.830
I'm really surprised that Pops was doing something like that, and I want to know who sent the tape.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.470
But racking our brains now won't help us.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:43.530
What really interests me, though, is Europe.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:44.930
Takao?

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.890
Thanks to the video, I'm ever more fired up.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.090
I want to see these guys no matter what.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:53.200
Professor, I'm going to travel around Europe.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.310
Alone, if that's what it takes.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:58.010
Y-You can't do that! The Finals
are right around the corner!

00:13:58.010 --> 00:14:00.170
Nothing you can say will change my mind.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:02.530
I'm not the only one getting impatient here.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.290
Dragoon feels the same way.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.500
Takao...

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.300
That guy..!

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:30.100
What's the big idea?!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.590
The World Tournament...

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:36.520
I'll destroy it.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.120
What did you just say?!

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.530
He wants to destroy the World Tournament?!

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:42.790
What's this about?!

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:47.900
Wait, come back!

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:50.460
Give back my Dragoon!

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.630
There he is!

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:12.560
Dragoon!

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:29.120
W-What the heck is this?!

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:31.170
A-A mummy..?!

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:33.640
The Bit! The Bit is glowing..!

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:35.210
Don't tell me..!

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:38.840
It's a Sacred Beast?! Impossible! I've never seen a Sacred Beast like this!

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:46.740
Stop it! What are you doing to my Dragoon?!

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.070
Takao, move!

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:50.920
We'll save Dragoon!

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.720
Wait! Don't rush it!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.720
Go... Shoot!

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:07.290
It's coming after us!

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:08.600
Don't let it catch you!

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.100
How obstinate!

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:17.600
This is bad... The alleyway is too narrow.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:18.960
We can't dodge it like this!

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:22.210
Maybe... he brought us to the alley on purpose?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.340
You mean we were lured in here by him?!

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.510
Oh no!

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.890
Max, let's do this.

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:27.850
<i>Yes!</i>

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:41.460
<i>What?!</i>

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.010
How..? It can't be!

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:49.500
No way! He caught Byakko and Genbu?!

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:53.700
I've never... In my life, I've
never seen a fight like this!

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.570
Tsk! Those clumsy idiots.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:04.340
At this rate, he'll get Draciel and Driger, too..!

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:05.470
Stop it!

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:12.090
I will destroy all Beys in the World Tournament.

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.460
Not yet.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:18.020
There's still one Bey here.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:19.420
Kai!

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.400
If he keeps running...

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:49.500
He'll be caught!

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.400
Not exactly.

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:53.600
I think I know why Dranzer is moving like that!

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:00.780
Yes, that's it! Keep coming after me!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:13.990
I get it!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.870
That Kai! He made the bandages go after him...

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.280
so that the mummy would entangle itself!

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.060
What a smart tactic!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:27.710
Fire Arrow!

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:38.940
Dragoon!

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.970
Thank goodness you're okay.

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:47.380
This must be one of the Evil
Sacred Beasts mentioned in the video.

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:52.730
Where are you?! Show yourself!

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.250
Who or what are you?

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:17.790
What?!

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:29.090
I will crush you without fail.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.220
He disappeared...

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.260
W-What just happened?!

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:52.930
Who in the world was that guy?

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:54.870
He was a lot like an apparition.

00:19:55.780 --> 00:20:00.980
Europe might turn out to be
a gathering place for evil spirits.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:04.600
Takao?

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:08.930
What are you laughing at now?

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.780
Don't you think it's cool?

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:14.330
I mean, sure, that guy was creepy.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:18.690
But he was so strong!
And then there's Ralf Jurgens, too.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.410
All the more reason to want to explore Europe!

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:24.930
You're still on about that?! I told you, no way!

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:27.160
We can't have a repeat of what happened today!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.430
Wait a second, Professor.

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:33.100
I've decided to explore Europe with Takao.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.570
I'm going, too.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.580
Rei! Max!

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.630
Bladers who hate the Tournament...

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:40.300
I can't simply ignore that.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:43.050
Someone needs to do something about it.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:45.340
My fighting spirit is burning up!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.570
You sure know how to make me happy.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.770
I can't believe it... You too?

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:52.560
I'll go as well.

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:56.100
It should help us kill time on the way there.

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:57.700
Oh, jeez!

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:00.290
What do you say, Professor?

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:06.020
Very well. But be sure to get to our destination on time.

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:08.620
I won't allow any other detours!

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.500
Man, what am I going to tell President Daitenji..?

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:24.020
Europe... This is going to be a fun journey.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.720
Spring waves its hand smiling,

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:50.200
Summer spreads passion.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.350
Seasons pass one after the other,

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.560
Fall and Winter are good friends.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.660
When there is a problem you can't solve,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:11.560
Trust, friendship, love and emotion

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:18.800
Clouds keep flying across the sky,

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:24.200
the sky keeps changing every second

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:29.090
My eyes well up and tears stream down my face,

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:33.090
but they're not tears of sadness

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:39.420
I summon my courage and try to put it into words.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.770
"Let's go on a journey to the city of hope!"

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.760
All your dreams will come true

00:22:57.860 --> 00:23:01.120
According to my analysis, <i>oh, dangerous!</i>

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:04.040
The Mummy's Sacred Beast... It's Europe, after all.

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:06.500
No, no, it's still too soon to be scared!

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:11.520
Waiting for us in a long and dark tunnel was...

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:15.990
Roar! The Sacred Beasts of the Werewolf and Vampire!

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:19.840
Next time: The Dark Bladers Attack!

00:23:19.840 --> 00:23:24.090
Oh come on! Dark this, dark that... this is no walk in the park!
